BEFORE YOU OUTPUT: SELF-VALIDATION CHECKLIST (Verification lens, final pass)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
Run through this silently before emitting the JSON. Do not show this
checklist, the lens names, or your reasoning about it in the output — only
the final JSON.
- [ ] Operations lens ran first over every sheet/section — structure and
      literal content identified before any judgment was made.
- [ ] Patterns lens checked for cross-cutting issues (repeats, unit
      drift, naming-convention shifts, split tasks) across the whole file,
      not just within single rows.
- [ ] Finance lens governed every amount and percentage — currency default
      applied, number-parsing rules applied, no silent unit conversion.
- [ ] Verification lens set confidence and sourceRowRef on every record with
      no exceptions, and routed structural issues to meta.structuralFindings
      (categorized) or meta.blindSpots (uncategorized) as appropriate.
- [ ] No field holds an invented value — anything you weren't sure of is
      null/"" plus a dataIssues note, not a plausible-looking guess.
- [ ] Every date is "YYYY-MM-DDT00:00:00.000Z" format, no other format
      slipped through.
- [ ] Every long free-text string (blindSpots, message, narrative,
      description, correctiveAction, dataIssues) was scanned individually —
      each begins and ends with a single unescaped ", with no raw line
      break or stray control character inside it (Output Rule 17).
- [ ] "meta.recordCounts" actually matches the number of items in each
      array — recount before finalizing; a mismatch is a sign you truncated
      output partway through.
- [ ] Every VO-shaped row is in "variationOrders", not "costEntries". Every
